  "question": {
    "text": "A balloon has a volume 400 ml at <math><mn>0</mn><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> . The balloon is distended to 4/5th of its maximum stretching capacity.<br />\r(i) Will burst if it is brought into a room at <math><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> ?<br />\r(ii) What is the maximum temperature above which it will burst?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YXPzT",
      "text": "Balloon will not burst at <math><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> C, balloon will burst above 40 <math><mo>°</mo></math> C",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3sa3Z",
      "text": "Balloon will burst at <math><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> C, balloon will not burst above 68.25 <math><mo>°</mo></math> C",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ttOd4",
      "text": "Balloon will not burst at <math><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> C, balloon will burst above 68.25 <math><mo>°</mo></math> C",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "rsq9D",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) Maximum stretching capacity <math><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></math> ml<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br />or <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>273</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>313</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>458.61</mn></math> ml<br />If the volume becomes more than 500 ml it will burst. The volume is below 500 ml, hence it will not burst at 40 <math><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> .<br />(ii) <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br />or <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>273</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>500</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>341.25</mn></math> K = 68.25 <math><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math><br />The temperature at which the volume becomes 500 ml the balloon will burst. So balloon burst above 68.26 <math><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.",
